Basically, to make mysql client of iOS...

Unzip the files.

Change directory to the src directory.
cd mysql-connector-c-6.1.6-src

Run cmake to generate the Xcode project.
cmake -G Xcode -DIPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=7.0 -DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING -WITH_SSL="/Users/michael/Desktop/Reports/opt/lib/openssl"

Open in Xcode.

Change the valid archs to contain "i386 x86_64 armv7 armv7s arm64" for all static library projects.

May need to build comp_err for OS X first, and install it on your system in /usr/local/bin

May need to edit the Gen Error targets scripts to point to the local bin.

For each iphonesimulator and iphoneos, build both debug ("testing") and release ("profiling").

Lipo the files togeather and move the output files to ./opt/lib/mysqlclient/. and ./opt/lib/mysqlclient/Debug/.

